 HTTP Status Codes Every DevOps Engineer Must Know! 💻⚙️



✅ 2xx – Success

🔹 200 OK – Request succeeded. The bread and butter of web responses. 🍞
🔹 201 Created – Resource successfully created (think: POST /user). 🛠️
🔹 204 No Content – Success, but no content returned (DELETE ops!). 🧹


⚠️ 4xx – Client Errors

❌ 400 Bad Request – Malformed request. Usually a client-side mistake. 🧩
🚫 401 Unauthorized – Missing or invalid auth credentials. 🔐
🚷 403 Forbidden – Valid creds, but access is still denied (RBAC, IAM misconfigs). 🧱
❓ 404 Not Found – Requested resource doesn’t exist. Double-check URLs! 🔍
📦 429 Too Many Requests – You’re being rate-limited! Slow down! 🐢


🔥 5xx – Server Errors

💥 500 Internal Server Error – Catch-all error. Dive into logs ASAP! 🪵
🚒 502 Bad Gateway – Server got an invalid response from the upstream (LB ↔️ App). 🛤️
🧯 503 Service Unavailable – Service is overloaded or down for maintenance. ⏳
🔁 504 Gateway Timeout – Upstream didn’t respond in time. Troubleshoot backend. ⏱️
